 "sections": [
  {
   "name": "How Your Car Is Built to Crash",
   "lines": [
    [
     "c08_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "Your car is *designed* to crush",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "wow",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "crash"
      }
     },
     "Your car is designed to crush in a crash. On purpose. Here is why."
    ],
    [
     "c08_2",
     {
      "label": "old way",
      "head": "Old way: *body on frame*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "frame"
      }
     },
     "Older cars, and many trucks, bolt the body onto a heavy steel ladder frame. Tough, but heavy."
    ],
    [
     "c08_3",
     {
      "label": "new way",
      "head": "Most cars: *monocoque*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "mono"
      }
     },
     "Most modern cars use a monocoque, or unibody. The body shell itself is the frame. Lighter and stiffer."
    ],
    [
     "c08_4",
     {
      "label": "crumple",
      "head": "*Crumple zones* absorb the hit",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "crash"
      }
     },
     "The front and back are built to fold up in a crash, soaking up energy, so your body does not have to."
    ],
    [
     "c08_5",
     {
      "label": "cage",
      "head": "The cabin is a *safety cage*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "crash"
      }
     },
     "The passenger cell uses ultra high strength steel, built to keep its shape around you."
    ],
    [
     "c08_6",
     {
      "label": "physics",
      "head": "Slower stop, *smaller* force",
      "pose": "think",
      "face": "think",
      "prop": {
       "type": "versus",
       "a": {
        "t": "RIGID CAR",
        "big": "sudden",
        "sub": "huge forces"
       },
       "b": {
        "t": "CRUMPLE ZONE",
        "big": "gradual",
        "sub": "lower forces"
       },
       "win": "b"
      }
     },
     "Crumpling makes the stop take a little longer. Spreading it out over more time means much lower forces on you."
    ],
    [
     "c08_7",
     {
      "label": "restraints",
      "head": "Belts and airbags *finish* the job",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "checklist",
       "items": [
        [
         "Crumple zones",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Safety cage",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Seatbelts",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Airbags",
         true
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "Seatbelts and airbags hold you in place, while the car absorbs the crash around you."
    ],
    [
     "c08_8",
     {
      "label": "takeaway",
      "head": "Crushed car, *safe* people",
      "pose": "thumbs",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "crash"
      }
     },
     "A crushed car is often a car that did its job."
    ]
   ]
  }
